# Production-ready bar

Implementation is not done until it is safe to ship to paying churches on Vercel. Align with ISO/IEC 25010: it must work, be secure, reliable, maintainable, and usable — not merely demoable.

## Definition of done

- Correct for the PRD (SaaS tenant isolation, zones ≠ churches, attendance is counts).
- Typed, validated input and explicit errors. No `any`, no swallowed exceptions.
- Authz on the server. UI hiding is not security.
- Tests for the risk you introduced (especially tenant/zone isolation).
- No secrets in git, client bundles, or logs.
- No unfinished feature flags that expose incomplete APIs.

## Do not

```ts
// ❌ ship this
} catch (e) {}
fetch('/api/v1/members') // no session / no error handling
```

```ts
// ✅
} catch (e) {
  logger.error('members.list_failed', { churchId, error: e });
  throw e;
}
```

If a change cannot meet this bar, do not merge it; narrow the scope instead.
